// O04-ARMS — the additional declared callee premises the caller's remaining
// early-return arms traverse. Concatenated onto `o04_path.qcore`, which stays
// byte-unchanged so card O04's own measurement keeps its exact premise set.
//
// EVERY declaration here is a TRUSTED ASSUMPTION, exactly like O04's. Neither
// is derived from any body in this fixture, and neither is offered as a
// production declaration: this file lives with the gateway test fixtures, so
// the pinned `contract/qcore` corpus count is untouched.
//
// O00 §8 feature P3 predicted three logging entry points (`flb_log_check`,
// `flb_log_print`, `flb_errno_print`). In the byte-verbatim upstream region the
// caller writes `flb_error(...)`, the macro those three expand from, so the
// prediction collapses to one declaration here. The second declaration
// (`flb_routes_mask_get_size`) was NOT in P3's list and was found by
// re-measurement; `flb_time_now`, the third uncontracted callee the arms
// traverse, is measured *inert* — its statement is an indirect store that
// refuses before any contract is consulted — and is deliberately left
// undeclared rather than declared for appearances.

// --- the logging expansion ------------------------------------------------
// Premise: the error-logging entry point borrows every argument and returns no
// custody.
//
// This declaration used to name three parameters — the arity of this call site
// — because the vocabulary then had no variadic-tail form, and it was recorded
// as the named follow-on O04-ARMS-VARIADIC. Card O04-TRACE added the tail
// clause, and card **LOADER-ABI** measured that the three-parameter form
// disagrees with C's `void flb_error(const char *format, ...)`: the declaration
// named modes for two parameters the C declaration never typed. It is now the
// faithful one-parameter-plus-tail form, which is what `flb_trace` already
// uses; the arity disagreement is refused rather than believed.
extern fn flb_error(format: ptr<const, u8>) -> unit
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(format);
    ensures normal resource_variadic_data_tail();
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

// --- the routes-mask sizing helper ----------------------------------------
// Premise: sizing the routes mask borrows the router and returns a scalar.
extern fn flb_routes_mask_get_size(router: ptr<mut, u8>) -> u64
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(router);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
